# Backend (NestJS) Conventions

## Module pattern

Each domain is a NestJS module under `backend/src/`:
`controller` → HTTP + Swagger decorators · `service` → business logic · `dto/` → validation

## Auth & roles

```typescript
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)
@Roles(UserRole.PROJECT_MANAGER, UserRole.PROGRAMMING_HEAD)
```

- `@Public()` skips JWT on auth endpoints
- `@CurrentUser()` injects authenticated user
- Role filtering belongs in the **service**, not only the controller

## Ticket actions checklist

When adding/modifying ticket transitions:

1. Validate current status allows the transition
2. Write `TicketStatusHistory` record
3. Call `AuditService.log(...)`
4. Send notification via `NotificationsService`
5. Send email via `EmailService` when user-facing

## Prisma

- Use `PrismaService` (injected globally)
- Prisma 7 uses `@prisma/adapter-pg` — see `backend/src/prisma/prisma.service.ts`
- Migrations: `npx prisma migrate dev --name <name>` from `backend/`

## DTOs

- Use `class-validator` decorators on all request DTOs
- Export enums from DTO files when shared (e.g. `ApprovalDecision`)
- Swagger: `@ApiTags`, `@ApiBearerAuth`, `@ApiOperation`

## Errors

- `NotFoundException` — missing entity
- `ForbiddenException` — role/ownership violation
- `BadRequestException` — invalid status transition or input
